{"timestamp":"2026-10-31T18:32:48.149Z","ordinal":12,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a19336-7aab-7cb2-b50a-7c1a49be3375","turn_id":"01a1933c-5738-7731-8759-a76efb94470d","item":{"type":"UserMessage","id":"01a1933c-5914-72d3-b184-f3f7b5aac0f0","client_id":"fd8f3f0c-724b-4ceb-aecc-5e65a3e57f18","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a UI test of the chat view you are shown in. Work only in /work (create it) and touch no repo. Do every step in order and don't stop to ask unless a step says so.\n\n1. Make a task list with one item per step below and keep it current as you go.\n2. Think it through first, then write one reply that uses every markdown feature: h1, h2 and h3; bold, italic, strikethrough and inline code; a link; a blockquote holding a nested list; ordered, unordered and nested lists; a task list with done and open items; a table with left, center and right aligned columns and inline code in a cell; a horizontal rule; code blocks in rust, python, bash, json and diff; one line longer than 300 characters; an emoji; and a footnote.\n3. Draw two mermaid diagrams in mermaid code blocks: a flowchart with a decision and a subgraph, and a sequence diagram with three participants and an alt block.\n4. Tool calls: write three small files, read one back, edit one, glob them and grep them for a word. Run one bash command that fails on purpose (exit 3), one that prints 200 lines, and fetch https://example.com.\n5. Start `for i in $(seq 1 20); do echo tick $i; sleep 1; done` as a background shell task. Keep working and read its output at the end.\n6. Launch three subagents at once: one counts the lines in the files, one writes a haiku about terminals, and one runs `sleep 15` in bash and then reports back. Then launch a fourth subagent in the background and collect its result at the end.\n7. Ask me a multiple-choice question with three options using your question tool, and wait for my answer.\n8. Run `zz list-panes -a -F '#{session_name} #{window_index} #{pane_id}'` and `echo $ZZ_PANE`. Then mention in plain prose the pane you run in, another pane, its window, its session, a file with a line number, and a folder, both as zz references (@host:$session:window.%pane) and as plain paths.\n9. Finish with a summary table of what each step did and a mermaid pie chart of roughly how long each step took.","text_elements":[]}]},"started_at_ms":1793471568148,"completed_at_ms":1793471568149}}
